The attached image shows that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response at the injection site and is taken up by recruited cells, following intramuscular injection of Nano-11 combined with ovalbumin. Panel A plots the number of various inflammatory cells over time, indicating a peak in Mac-2+ macrophages and Ly6C+ monocytes around day 2, with fewer neutrophils. Panel B displays confocal microscopy images at different time points, demonstrating that Nano-11 (red) is internalized by MHCII+, Ly6C+, Mac-2+, and 1A8+ cells (green), confirming cellular uptake by various myeloid cell types and the transient nature of the local inflammation.